  "frontier_coordinate": "R-134 proves the sharp six-row floor residual and, after exhaustive output clusters are placed in one direct sum under each root-spatial owner, the root/visit-free fixed-law action lower bound. Separate A^2 plus B_e^2 payment is cutoff-divergent. Pointwise six-real terminal ellipticity gives exact negative moments and sub-fourth quotient-jet bounds; the embedded Pauli fourth jet has a positive-floor fixed-cone logarithmic divergence. A unit-covariance high-frequency Gaussian field proves that pointwise ellipticity alone does not imply spatial fractional control. Conditional on the R-092 joint spatial hypotheses, an owner-preserving R-087-self-atom to R-088-sequential-atom transfer, and a one-use q_k ledger, the gamma=7/12 geometric summation has exact square constant 0.6588816258726145 and direct fixed-collar constant 0.28592888585547915. The live successor is A13-CLASSII-SIGNED-FOREST-TERMINAL-INNOVATION-ONE-USE-HEADROOM-BOUND: prove those production bridges while retaining the signed forest-current combination, then establish near/balanced headroom, production shell constants, matching energy, strict gap, and the absolute anchor before applying R-129. OVERLAP_src, Nelson, removals, interacting measure, and Sector A remain open.",
